::GATE 2024 Set 2 Q26::[plain]Which of the following file organizations is/are I/O efficient for the scan operation in DBMS? {~%50.0%Sorted ~%50.0%Heap ~%-100%Unclustered tree index ~%-100%Unclustered hash index}
####Source: GATE 2024 Set 2, Q26

::GATE 2024 Set 2 Q27::[plain]Which of the following statements about the Two Phase Locking (2PL) protocol is/are TRUE? {~%33.33%2PL permits only serializable schedules ~%-100%With 2PL, a transaction always locks the data item being read or written just before every operation and always releases the lock just after the operation ~%33.33%With 2PL, once a lock is released on any data item inside a transaction, no more locks on any data item can be obtained inside that transaction ~%33.33%A deadlock is possible with 2PL}
####Source: GATE 2024 Set 2, Q27

::GATE 2024 Set 2 Q45::[plain]The relation schema, Person(pid,city), describes the city of residence for every person uniquely identified by pid. The following relational algebra operators are available\: selection, projection, cross product, and rename. To find the list of cities where at least 3 persons reside, using the above operators, the minimum number of cross product operations that must be used is {~1 =2 ~3 ~4}
####Source: GATE 2024 Set 2, Q45

::GATE 2024 Set 2 Q56::[plain]A functional dependency 𝐹\:⁡𝑋 → 𝑌 is termed as a useful functional dependency if and only if it satisfies all the following three conditions\: • 𝑋 is not the empty set. • 𝑌 is not the empty set. • Intersection of 𝑋 and 𝑌 is the empty set. For a relation 𝑅 with 4 attributes, the total number of possible useful functional dependencies is ________ {#50}
