::GATE 2025 Set 1 Q39::[plain]Consider two relations describing 𝑡𝑒𝑎𝑚𝑠 and 𝑝𝑙𝑎𝑦𝑒𝑟𝑠 in a sports league\: {=\{ 𝑝. 𝑝𝑛𝑎𝑚𝑒 | 𝑝 ∈ 𝑝𝑙𝑎𝑦𝑒𝑟𝑠 ∧ ∃𝑡 (𝑡 ∈ 𝑡𝑒𝑎𝑚𝑠 ∧ 𝑝. 𝑡𝑖𝑑 \= 𝑡. 𝑡𝑖𝑑 ∧ 𝑡. 𝑡𝑛𝑎𝑚𝑒 \= ′𝑀𝐼′)\} ~\{ 𝑝. 𝑝𝑛𝑎𝑚𝑒 | 𝑝 ∈ 𝑡𝑒𝑎𝑚𝑠 ∧ ∃𝑡 (𝑡 ∈ 𝑝𝑙𝑎𝑦𝑒𝑟𝑠 ∧ 𝑝. 𝑡𝑖𝑑 \= 𝑡. 𝑡𝑖𝑑 ∧ 𝑡. 𝑡𝑛𝑎𝑚𝑒 \= ′𝑀𝐼′)\} ~\{ 𝑝. 𝑝𝑛𝑎𝑚𝑒 | 𝑝 ∈ 𝑝𝑙𝑎𝑦𝑒𝑟𝑠 ∧ ∃𝑡 (𝑡 ∈ 𝑡𝑒𝑎𝑚𝑠 ∧ 𝑡. 𝑡𝑛𝑎𝑚𝑒 \= ′𝑀𝐼′)\} ~\{ 𝑝. 𝑝𝑛𝑎𝑚𝑒 | 𝑝 ∈ 𝑡𝑒𝑎𝑚𝑠 ∧ ∃𝑡 (𝑡 ∈ 𝑝𝑙𝑎𝑦𝑒𝑟𝑠 ∧ 𝑡. 𝑡𝑛𝑎𝑚𝑒 \= ′𝑀𝐼′)\}}
####Source: GATE 2025 Set 1, Q39

::GATE 2025 Set 1 Q47::[plain]Consider a relational schema 𝑡𝑒𝑎𝑚(𝑛𝑎𝑚𝑒, 𝑐𝑖𝑡𝑦, 𝑜𝑤𝑛𝑒𝑟), with functional dependencies \{𝑛𝑎𝑚𝑒 → 𝑐𝑖𝑡𝑦, 𝑛𝑎𝑚𝑒 → 𝑜𝑤𝑛𝑒𝑟\}. The relation 𝑡𝑒𝑎𝑚 is decomposed into two relations, 𝑡1(𝑛𝑎𝑚𝑒, 𝑐𝑖𝑡𝑦) and 𝑡2(𝑛𝑎𝑚𝑒, 𝑜𝑤𝑛𝑒𝑟). Which of the following statement(s) is/are TRUE? {~%-100%The relation 𝑡𝑒𝑎𝑚 is NOT in BCNF. ~%50.0%The relations 𝑡1 and 𝑡2 are in BCNF. ~%50.0%The decomposition constitutes a lossless join. ~%-100%The relation 𝑡𝑒𝑎𝑚 is NOT in 3NF.}
####Source: GATE 2025 Set 1, Q47

::GATE 2025 Set 1 Q55::[plain]Consider the following database tables of a sports league. player(pid,pname,age) coach(cid,cname) team(tid,tname,city,cid) members(pid,tid) An instance of the table and an SQL query are given. player coach team members SELECT MIN(P.age) FROM player P WHERE P.pid IN ( SELECT M.pid FROM team T, coach C, members M WHERE C.cname \= 'Mark' AND T.cid \= C.cid AND M.tid \= T.tid ) The value returned by the given SQL query is ______ . (Answer in integer) {#26}
####Source: GATE 2025 Set 1, Q55

::GATE 2025 Set 2 Q27::[plain]An audit of a banking transactions system has found that on an earlier occasion, two joint holders of account 𝐴 attempted simultaneous transfers of Rs. 10000 each from account 𝐴 to account 𝐵. Both transactions read the same value, Rs. 11000, as the initial balance in 𝐴 and were allowed to go through. 𝐵 was credited Rs. 10000 twice. 𝐴 was debited only once and ended up with a balance of Rs. 1000. Which of the following properties is/are certain to have been violated by the system? {~%-100%Atomicity ~%50.0%Consistency ~%50.0%Isolation ~%-100%Durability}
####Source: GATE 2025 Set 2, Q27

::GATE 2025 Set 2 Q46::[plain]Consider the following relational schema along with all the functional dependencies that hold on them. R1(A, B, C, D, E)\: \{ 𝐷 → 𝐸, 𝐸𝐴 → 𝐵, 𝐸𝐵 → 𝐶\} R2(A, B, C, D)\: \{ 𝐴 → 𝐷, 𝐴 → 𝐵, 𝐶 → 𝐴\} Which of the following statement(s) is/are TRUE? {~%-100%R1 is in 3NF ~%-100%R2 is in 3NF ~%50.0%R1 is NOT in 3NF ~%50.0%R2 is NOT in 3NF}
####Source: GATE 2025 Set 2, Q46

