::GATE 2023 Q26::[plain]Geetha has a conjecture about integers, which is of the form ∀x P (x) \=⇒ ∃yQ(x, y) , where P is a statement about integers, and Q is a statement about pairs of integers. Which of the following (one or more) option(s) would imply Geetha’s conjecture? {~%-100%∃x P (x) ∧ ∀yQ(x, y) ~%50.0%∀x∀yQ(x, y) ~%50.0%∃y∀x P (x) \=⇒ Q(x, y) ~%-100%∃x P (x) ∧ ∃yQ(x, y)}
####Source: GATE 2023, Q26

::GATE 2023 Q28::[plain]Let f (x) \= x3 + 15x2 − 33x − 36 be a real-valued function. Which of the following statements is/are TRUE? {~%-100%f (x) does not have a local maximum. ~%50.0%f (x) has a local maximum. ~%-100%f (x) does not have a local minimum. ~%50.0%f (x) has a local minimum.}
