::GATE 2024 Set 1 Q14::[plain]Consider a permutation sampled uniformly at random from the set of all permutations of \{1, 2, 3, ⋯ , 𝑛\} for some 𝑛 ≥ 4. Let 𝑋 be the event that 1 occurs before 2 in the permutation, and 𝑌 the event that 3 occurs before 4. Which one of the following statements is TRUE? {~The events 𝑋 and 𝑌 are mutually exclusive =The events 𝑋 and 𝑌 are independent ~Either event 𝑋 or 𝑌 must occur ~Event 𝑋 is more likely than event 𝑌}
