::GATE 2024 Set 1 Q51::[plain]The chromatic number of a graph is the minimum number of colours used in a proper colouring of the graph. Let 𝐺 be any graph with 𝑛 vertices and chromatic number 𝑘. Which of the following statements is/are always TRUE? {~%-100%𝐺 contains a complete subgraph with 𝑘 vertices ~%50.0%𝐺 contains an independent set of size at least 𝑛/𝑘 ~%50.0%𝐺 contains at least 𝑘(𝑘 − 1)/2 edges ~%-100%𝐺 contains a vertex of degree at least 𝑘}
