::GATE 2026 Set 2 Q38::[plain]Consider an array 𝐴 of integers of size 𝑛. The indices of 𝐴 run from 1 to 𝑛. An algorithm is to be designed to check whether 𝐴 satisfies the condition given below. ∀𝑖, 𝑗 ∈ \{1, … , 𝑛 − 1\} such that 𝑖 > 𝑗, (𝐴[𝑖 + 1] − 𝐴[𝑖]) > (𝐴[𝑗 + 1] − 𝐴[𝑗]) Which one of the following gives the worst case time complexity of the fastest algorithm that can be designed for the problem? {=Θ(𝑛) ~Θ(log(𝑛)) ~Θ(𝑛 log(𝑛)) ~Θ(𝑛2 )}
