::GATE 2023 Q40::[plain]Consider the pushdown automaton (PDA) P below, which runs on the input alphabet \{a, b\}, has stack alphabet \{⊥, A\}, and has three states \{s, p, q\}, with s being the start state. A transition from state u to state v, labelled c/X/γ, where c is an input symbol or , X is a stack symbol, and γ is a string of stack symbols, represents the fact that in state u, the PDA can read c from the input, with X on the top of its stack, pop X from the stack, push in the string γ on the stack, and go to state v. In the initial conﬁguration, the stack has only the symbol ⊥ in it. The PDA accepts by empty stack. a/⊥/A⊥ a/A/AA s b/A/ b/A/ /A/ p /A/ q /A/ /⊥/ Which one of the following options correctly describes the language accepted by P ? {=\{am bn | 1 ≤ m and n < m\} ~\{am bn | 0 ≤ n ≤ m\} ~\{am bn | 0 ≤ m and 0 ≤ n\} ~\{am | 0 ≤ m\} ∪ \{bn | 0 ≤ n\}}
####Source: GATE 2023, Q40

